## 12. ANTI-PATTERNS & COMMON MISTAKES

### ❌ AVOID THESE PATTERNS
- **Subjective Assessments:** Don't base findings on personal preferences
- **Generic Recommendations:** Avoid one-size-fits-all suggestions
- **Missing Context:** Don't ignore project-specific constraints
- **Over-Criticism:** Don't focus only on problems without acknowledging good practices
- **Incomplete Analysis:** Don't skip any of the five audit dimensions

### ✅ BEST PRACTICES
- **Evidence-Based:** Always reference specific code or patterns
- **Context-Aware:** Consider project constraints and requirements
- **Actionable:** Provide concrete steps for improvement
- **Balanced:** Acknowledge both strengths and areas for improvement
- **Professional:** Maintain objective, constructive tone

